{%- comment -%}
  Local Inventory Ads feed (Google Merchant Center "local product inventory").

  Renders a tab-delimited file with exactly four columns:
      id, store_code, availability, quantity

  Usage: bound to an alternate collection template so the source cohort is the
  collection in the URL, e.g.

      /collections/french-fitness-showroom-products?view=local-inventory-tsv

  Rules (per Tim, Sept 4 items 4.1-4.5 and Sept 5 item 4.6 resolution):
    - id            the offer ID the primary Google feed uses for that variant.
                    That is NOT always the SKU - see the id rule below.
                    One row per offer ID, deduplicated, no parent-product rows.
    - store_code    fixed, see STORE_CODE below.
    - availability  in_stock only when the variant is web-in-stock AND the
                    maximum stated processing time is MAX_LEAD_BUSINESS_DAYS
                    business days or less. Everything else out_of_stock.
                    Values are lowercase with an underscore.
    - quantity      0 whenever availability is out_of_stock. When in_stock, see
                    QUANTITY_MODE below.

  ID RULE - verified against the live googleshoppingfs and
  googleshoppingfrenchfitness exports on 2026-09-05. MultiFeeds does not use one
  scheme, it uses three, and a local row whose id does not match the primary
  offer ID processes as "Offer does not exist":

    1. Multi-variant product -> "<product.id>-<variant.id>". MultiFeeds keys
       every variant of a multi-variant product this way, so the SKU is wrong
       for all of them (45 rows in the current showroom cohort).
    2. Single-variant product carrying custom.old_legacy_product_code ->
       that legacy code. MultiFeeds keys the offer by the legacy code and puts
       the current SKU in old_id. Only FFT-CFDI does this today, keyed FFA-CFDI.
    3. Otherwise -> variant.sku. This covers the large majority.

  KNOWN LIMITATION - INCLUSION PARITY. This template emits a row for every
  variant in the collection, but the primary feed does not carry every one of
  them: 154 of the 420 variants in the showroom collection have no primary
  offer at all, and nothing visible in Shopify distinguishes them (they are
  ACTIVE, published, and span the same price range as included items - a $24
  dumbbell is in the feed while a $22 collar is not). The inclusion rule lives
  in the MultiFeeds source configuration, which Liquid cannot read. So this
  template alone cannot guarantee zero unmatched offers. Either point it at a
  collection that mirrors the primary feed's contents, or generate the local
  feed from the same MultiFeeds source that generates the primary feed.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign TAB = '	' -%}
{%- assign NL = '
' -%}

{%- comment -%} Merchant Center store code. Do not change without Tim's GO. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign STORE_CODE = 'FSS1' -%}

{%- comment -%} Two weeks, expressed in business days. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign MAX_LEAD_BUSINESS_DAYS = 10 -%}

{%- comment -%}
  QUANTITY_MODE:
    'stopgap' - emit 1 for in_stock and 0 for out_of_stock. This mirrors the
                interim fs_local_inventory_clean.tsv and avoids publishing
                Shopify's orderability numbers (9,989 / 449,511 / -9,999),
                which are not real shelf counts and would fail Google's
                inventory verification.
    'shopify' - emit variant.inventory_quantity. Only switch to this once
                Shopify carries real Benicia counts.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign QUANTITY_MODE = 'stopgap' -%}

{%- capture feed -%}
id{{ TAB }}store_code{{ TAB }}availability{{ TAB }}quantity
{%- assign seen_skus = '|' -%}
{%- paginate collection.products by 1000 -%}
  {%- for product in collection.products -%}
    {%- for variant in product.variants -%}

      {%- assign sku = variant.sku | strip -%}
      {%- if sku == blank -%}
        {%- continue -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} Offer ID, per the three-part ID RULE documented above. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if product.variants.size > 1 -%}
        {%- assign offer_id = product.id | append: '-' | append: variant.id -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- assign legacy_code = variant.metafields.custom.old_legacy_product_code.value | first | strip -%}
        {%- if legacy_code != blank -%}
          {%- assign offer_id = legacy_code -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- assign offer_id = sku -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- assign offer_key = '|' | append: offer_id | append: '|' -%}
      {%- if seen_skus contains offer_key -%}
        {%- continue -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- assign seen_skus = seen_skus | append: offer_id | append: '|' -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Processing Time source, most specific first. This is the field rendered
        on the PDP as "Processing Time".
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign lead_raw = variant.metafields.custom.processing_time_long_variant -%}
      {%- if lead_raw == blank -%}
        {%- assign lead_raw = product.metafields.custom.processing_time_long -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if lead_raw == blank -%}
        {%- assign lead_raw = product.metafields.custom.processing_time -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- assign lead = lead_raw | downcase | strip -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Parse the MAXIMUM stated lead time, in business days. "3-7 Business
        Days" yields 7, not 3. Weeks are converted at 5 business days per week.
        A blank or unparseable value yields -1, which never qualifies.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign lead_days = -1 -%}
      {%- if lead contains 'business day' -%}
        {%- assign lead_token = lead | split: 'business day' | first | strip | split: ' ' | last | split: '-' | last | strip -%}
        {%- assign lead_number = lead_token | times: 1 -%}
        {%- if lead_number > 0 -%}
          {%- assign lead_days = lead_number -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- elsif lead contains 'week' -%}
        {%- assign lead_token = lead | split: 'week' | first | strip | split: ' ' | last | split: '-' | last | strip -%}
        {%- assign lead_number = lead_token | times: 1 -%}
        {%- if lead_number > 0 -%}
          {%- assign lead_days = lead_number | times: 5 -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} Shopify quantity for the single Benicia location. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign tracked = true -%}
      {%- if variant.inventory_management == blank -%}
        {%- assign tracked = false -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- assign shopify_qty = variant.inventory_quantity | times: 1 -%}

      {%- assign availability = 'out_of_stock' -%}
      {%- if variant.available -%}
        {%- if lead_days > 0 and lead_days <= MAX_LEAD_BUSINESS_DAYS -%}
          {%- if tracked == false -%}
            {%- assign availability = 'in_stock' -%}
          {%- elsif shopify_qty > 0 -%}
            {%- assign availability = 'in_stock' -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Hard out_of_stock guards. These can only demote a row, never promote it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if lead contains 'restock' -%}
        {%- assign availability = 'out_of_stock' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- assign pt_filter = product.metafields.custom.processing_time_filter | downcase -%}
      {%- if pt_filter contains 'out of stock' -%}
        {%- assign availability = 'out_of_stock' -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- assign quantity = 0 -%}
      {%- if availability == 'in_stock' -%}
        {%- if QUANTITY_MODE == 'shopify' and tracked and shopify_qty > 0 -%}
          {%- assign quantity = shopify_qty -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- assign quantity = 1 -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {{- NL -}}{{- offer_id -}}{{- TAB -}}{{- STORE_CODE -}}{{- TAB -}}{{- availability -}}{{- TAB -}}{{- quantity -}}

    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endpaginate -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{{- feed | strip -}}
{{- NL -}}
